From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: allow re-attach of a PHY to the same netdev

phy_attach_direct() rejects any PHY that already has attached_dev set,
even when it is being attached to the very same net_device.  With DSA the
slave netdev can be set up (and thus the PHY attached) more than once, so
the second attempt fails with -EBUSY and the port never comes up.

Only treat it as a conflict when a *different* netdev already owns the
PHY, which is what the upstream driver does.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c	2026-10-09 19:43:35.135187403 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c	2026-10-09 19:43:35.135187403 +0800
@@ -1522,7 +1522,7 @@
 			goto error_module_put;
 	}
 
-	if (phydev->attached_dev) {
+	if (phydev->attached_dev && phydev->attached_dev != dev) {
 		dev_err(&dev->dev, "PHY already attached\n");
 		err = -EBUSY;
 		goto error;
